How to Find & Apply for Jobs Using Claude + LinkedIn + Naukri

Complete Step-by-Step Workflow

Overview
In this workflow, Claude is used as a job-search and application assistant. LinkedIn is the primary source of truth for your professional profile, while Naukri is used to find and apply to relevant job openings.

The complete flow is:
Install Claude Extension → Login to LinkedIn + Naukri → Open LinkedIn Profile → Open Claude Extension → Paste Prompt → Claude Analyzes Profile → Searches Naukri → Shortlists Jobs → Opens Jobs in Tabs → Review Jobs → Ask Claude to Apply → Review → Submit → Track Applications.

Step 1 — Install the Claude Chrome Extension
1. Open Google Chrome on your computer.
2. Open a new browser tab and go to Google.
3. Search for: “Claude Chrome Extension”.
4. Open the relevant Chrome Web Store result.
5. Click “Add to Chrome” and complete the installation.
6. Once installed, Claude will be available through the Chrome Extensions menu.

Step 2 — Login to LinkedIn and Naukri
Both LinkedIn and Naukri must be logged in within the same Chrome browser.

LinkedIn:
• Log in to LinkedIn.
• Open your complete LinkedIn profile.
• Make sure your profile contains your About section, experience, skills, projects, education, certifications, achievements, technologies, job titles and other relevant information.

Naukri:
• Open Naukri.com in another tab.
• Log in to your Naukri account.
• Keep the session active before starting the Claude workflow.

This is important because Claude needs access to the logged-in browser session when navigating between the two websites.

Step 3 — Open Your LinkedIn Profile
Go to your own LinkedIn profile.

LinkedIn should be treated as the primary source of truth for understanding your professional background.

Claude should use the profile to understand:
• Total experience
• Current role
• Previous companies and roles
• Technical skills
• Programming languages
• Frameworks
• Cloud technologies
• Databases
• Projects
• Certifications
• Education
• Achievements
• Domain experience
• Profile keywords
• Seniority

Step 4 — Open the Claude Extension
1. While you are on your LinkedIn profile, go to the top-right corner of Chrome.
2. Click the Extensions icon (puzzle-piece icon).
3. Find the Claude extension.
4. Click Claude.
5. Claude will open in a browser side window.

You are now ready to give Claude the job-search instructions.

Step 5 — Paste the Master Job Search Prompt
Before pressing Enter, make sure:
• LinkedIn is logged in.
• Naukri is logged in.
• You are currently on your LinkedIn profile.
• Claude Extension is open.

Replace [ROLE] with the role you want to target and [LOCATION] with your preferred location.

Example:
ROLE: SDE 3
LOCATION: Bangalore

Then paste the following prompt:

Use my LinkedIn profile as the primary source of truth. Analyze my complete profile, including work experience, technical skills, projects, certifications, education, achievements, and keywords.

Based on this analysis, search Naukri.com for job openings for [ROLE] in [LOCATION] that satisfy all of the following conditions:

• Posted within the last 24 hours.
• Have fewer than 50 applicants, wherever applicant count is available.
• Strongly match my experience, skills, and profile keywords.
• Avoid weak matches.
• Prioritize jobs that maximize my chances of getting shortlisted.
• Exclude duplicate listings.
• Exclude expired listings.

For each matching job, provide:

• Job Title
• Company Name
• Location
• Salary, if available
• Experience Required
• Applicant Count, if available
• Why it matches my profile
• Matching skills
• Missing skills, if any
• Match Score
• Direct Naukri application link
• Job posting date

Rank the jobs from best match to least match and return only high-confidence matches.

Use the actual job description to evaluate the match rather than relying only on the job title.

Compare my LinkedIn profile against the actual requirements, responsibilities, technologies, experience level, and seniority mentioned in each job description.

Do not include a job merely because it contains a few keywords from my profile.

Optimize the ranking for:

Probability of getting shortlisted > keyword similarity > number of available jobs.

If there are only a few high-confidence matches, return only those matches. Do not include weak jobs just to increase the number of results.

Verify that each job is still active before including it in the final list.

After identifying the high-confidence jobs, open the shortlisted job listings in separate browser tabs so I can review them.

Step 6 — Press Enter
Once you have pasted the prompt, press Enter.

Claude will:
1. Analyze your LinkedIn profile.
2. Understand your experience and skills.
3. Open/search Naukri.
4. Search for the specified role.
5. Filter according to location.
6. Check recently posted jobs.
7. Check applicant count where available.
8. Compare job descriptions with your LinkedIn profile.
9. Remove weak matches.
10. Remove duplicates.
11. Remove expired jobs.
12. Rank the strongest opportunities.
13. Give you the final shortlist.
14. Open the shortlisted jobs in separate browser tabs.

Step 7 — Claude Opens Relevant Jobs
After finding the relevant jobs, Claude can open shortlisted listings in separate browser tabs.

You may have:
• Tab 1: LinkedIn Profile
• Tab 2: Naukri
• Tab 3: Job 1
• Tab 4: Job 2
• Tab 5: Job 3
• Additional tabs for other shortlisted jobs

Claude should also provide the job details in its response.

Step 8 — Analyze the Shortlisted Jobs
Review every shortlisted job.

Check:
• Job title — Does it match the role you want?
• Company — Is it a company you are interested in?
• Location — Does the location work for you?
• Experience — Does the required experience fit?
• Technical skills — How much of the required stack do you already know?
• Responsibilities — Does the actual work match your background?
• Applicant count — Prefer lower applicant counts when other factors are comparable.

Do not rely only on keyword overlap. A job containing Java, AWS or Spring Boot is not automatically a strong match if the actual responsibilities are significantly different from your experience.

Step 9 — Ask Claude to Re-Rank Jobs
You can ask Claude:

“Analyze these shortlisted jobs again and tell me which ones have the highest probability of getting me shortlisted. Rank them from highest probability to lowest probability and explain why.”

This gives you a second-level review before applying.

Step 10 — Decide Which Jobs to Apply To
Do not blindly apply to every job Claude finds.

Select the jobs you are genuinely interested in.

For example:
“Apply to Job 1, Job 3, Job 5 and Job 7.”

Or:
“I want to apply only to jobs where my profile match is above 85% and where the core technical requirements match my experience.”

Step 11 — Ask Claude to Apply
Once you have approved the jobs, tell Claude:

“Apply to the shortlisted jobs that I have approved.

Use my existing Naukri profile information.

Do not fabricate or modify any information about my experience, education, skills, companies, projects, or achievements.

If any application asks a question that requires information not available in my profile, stop and ask me before submitting.

Before final submission, show me what will be submitted for each application.”

Claude can then navigate through the Naukri application flow.

Step 12 — Review Before Final Submission
Before allowing Claude to submit an application, review:
• Company
• Job title
• Location
• Resume
• Experience
• Notice period
• Expected salary
• Skills
• Application questions
• Any additional information

If everything is correct, allow Claude to proceed.

For questions requiring a personalized or subjective answer, review the answer yourself before submission.

Step 13 — Submit the Application
Once everything is verified, Claude can complete the application process for the approved job.

After successful submission, record:
• Company
• Job title
• Location
• Date applied
• Job URL
• Match score
• Applicant count
• Important notes

Step 14 — Repeat the Process
Repeat the workflow whenever you want to search for new opportunities.

Example:

Target Role: SDE 3
Location: Bangalore

Later:

Target Role: Staff Software Engineer
Location: Hyderabad

Or:

Target Role: Senior Backend Engineer
Location: Pune

The LinkedIn profile remains the source of truth, while role and location can change depending on your target opportunities.

Step 15 — Application Quality Rules
1. LinkedIn is the Source of Truth
Claude should primarily use your LinkedIn profile to understand your professional background.

2. Do Not Apply to Weak Matches
The goal is not to apply to hundreds of jobs. The goal is to identify jobs where you have a high probability of getting shortlisted.

3. Do Not Fabricate Information
Claude should never invent experience, skills, certifications, projects, job titles, companies, education or achievements.

4. Verify Before Submission
Claude can help automate the process, but you should retain control over final submission, especially for questions requiring personal or subjective answers.

5. Prefer Quality Over Quantity
Use:
LinkedIn Profile → Strong Job Matching → High-Confidence Shortlist → Review → Apply

rather than:
Search → Apply to Everything.

